  <name>Outlook for Linux</name>
  <summary>Unofficial Microsoft Outlook client for Linux</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Use the Microsoft Outlook web app as a standalone desktop application. Outlook for Linux wraps the Outlook web app in Electron and adds desktop integration such as system notifications, a tray unread badge, global shortcuts and spellcheck.</p>
    <p>It supports multiple accounts through separate profiles and helps with work sign-in flows, including Intune single sign-on, FIDO2 security keys and client certificates.</p>
    <p>This application is an unofficial client and is not affiliated with Microsoft.</p>
  </description>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/Taylor8484/outlook-for-linux</url>
